The independent semantic check agrees with the manifest classification: the empty case and constructor-decreasing recurrence match the supplied string iteration, membership, Boolean-to-integer addition, and parity-toggle semantics. Across 3,122 finite summary/operational comparisons there were no mismatches, while constant, all-index, pre-toggle, and lowercase-inclusive mutations were all detected. The decisive basis remains the source semantics; those tests are supporting evidence.
